cluster: tune the reduced single services workload

Select smaller MySQL workspaces, one API worker and a four-child nested
WebUI pool only for the single 2048 MiB services profile. Suppress the two
metrics export timers while retaining their services and essential tasks.

Keep normal and other-topology defaults, guest resources and source
contracts unchanged. These are qualification targets rather than a total
memory cap; applying them requires a newly prepared guest artifact.
